ass","severity":null,"notes":"THREE SUBSTANTIVE FINDINGS, all out of criterion. (1) MECHANISM CONTRADICTED BY CONVENTION D. The closing explanation \u2014 'the Markov trace of a confined baryon is negative because the Borromean braid B_3 carries odd parity under the sign representation of S_3' \u2014 cannot be the mechanism under production convention D. I verified symbolically that with z = q^3/(q^2+1) the Ocneanu hook-content weight vanishes on every lambda with l(lambda) >= 3 for all n <= 7, and (1^3) IS the sign representation, so y_{(1^3)} = 0 exactly: tr_M annihilates the sign channel. This is the same fact the sibling block markov-trace-frobenius-selection.md derives as the row cap. The sign of tr_M must come from the two-row channels, not from sign-representation parity. (2) NUMERIC CONTRADICTION WITH A SIBLING BLOCK. This block gives tr_M(proton) ~ -0.012 and tr_M(neutron) ~ -0.134; markov-trace-frobenius-selection.md gives tr_M(proton) = 1.0653061442544499 and tr_M(neutron) = 0.9232332299116371 at the proton pin. Not a convention rescaling \u2014 z_D/z_C = 1.2270, so no power of it carries +1.065 to -0.012. Worse for the argument here, the sibling's values give |tr_M(p)| > |tr_M(n)|, i.e. the OPPOSITE ordering to the one this block concludes. The two may be different braid words, but both are labelled tr_M(proton)/tr_M(neutron) at q_0 and they cannot both support the m_n > m_p conclusion. (3) PIN CURRENCY: 'q_0 = 1.109978595554181... (muon pin, 16 dps)' is the OLD muon value (current CAL-2 pin 1.10997859555733471, diverging at the 12th significant digit), and the 2026-08-07 owner directive defaults compute to the proton pin 1.1099785827513808. Same defect as mass-element-nf.md, so it is a chapter-level pattern rather than a one-off.","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:v02","model":null,"at":"2026-08-21","stale":true,"history":2},{"id":"trap-performed-warmth","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"Good practice: the CODATA comparison uses :val